# What every `.ax` file in the tree formats to: sha256(source) sha256(formatted) path.
#
# Materialized from the Rust compiler at commit 1041f11 on 2026-08-08, and
# verified at that commit to be IDENTICAL, all 224 mappings, to what the
# self-hosted compiler built from self_host/main.ax produces. That agreement is
# the provenance of this file, recorded on the last day there were two compilers
# to compare; check-fmt-selfhost.sh has held the self-hosted one to it since.
#
# KEYED BY THE SOURCE HASH, NOT THE PATH, and the path is diagnostic only. `fmt`
# rewrites 221 of these 224 files, so their formatted bytes move whenever anyone
# edits anything, and a golden that churns on every edit gets re-blessed unread.
# Hashing the input means an edited or deleted file RETIRES its entry - the gate
# joins on the source hash and only checks what it still covers - while an
# unedited file is pinned exactly. The floor on surviving entries (150 of 224)
# is what stops retirement from emptying the table into a vacuum.
#
# A hash rather than the bytes because the bytes are 1.4 MB and nobody reviews
# 1.4 MB. What the normal form LOOKS like is reviewed in
# tests/fmt/syntax-zoo.expected.ax and tests/fmt/parity.golden; this file is
# only the claim that it did not move.
#
# Regenerate deliberately, never automatically - a re-bless is how a broken
# formatter becomes the reference:
#
#   axc=$(mktemp -d)/axc
#   .axiom-bin/axiom build --input self_host/main.ax --output "$axc"
#   t=$(mktemp -d)
#   for f in $(find stdlib self_host tests -name '*.ax' | sort); do
#     cp "$f" "$t/c.ax"
#     h=$(shasum -a 256 "$f" | cut -d' ' -f1)
#     if "$axc" fmt "$t/c.ax" >/dev/null 2>&1
#       then printf '%s %s %s\n' "$h" "$(shasum -a 256 "$t/c.ax" | cut -d' ' -f1)" "$f"
#       else printf '%s REFUSED %s\n' "$h" "$f"; fi
#   done
#
# and keep this header. The gate's preservation and rebuild halves do not read
# this file, so they still fail on a formatter re-blessed while wrong.
#
#
# REGENERATED 2026-08-15, deliberately, at 354 entries from 224, after the
# printing work rewrote 445 call sites and retired 83 source hashes at once.
#
# REGENERATED again 2026-08-22, at 451 entries from 354, and this time the
# decay was invisible to every floor in the gate. 308 of the 354 entries still
# matched a file - comfortably above the 250 hit floor - while 143 of the 451
# `.ax` files in the tree had no entry at all, INCLUDING 17 of the 22 compiler
# sources. The table was healthy by every number it reported and had stopped
# covering the code the formatter is most likely to break. The gate now prints
# the unpinned count as well, so that shape is visible before it matters.
#
# Verified before blessing, and this is the check that makes a re-bless safe:
# of the 308 source hashes present in BOTH tables, zero mapped to a different
# formatted hash. So this is a re-keying of files that were edited, not a
# re-blessing of a formatter that moved. `self_host/format.ax` is unchanged in
# the commit that regenerates this.
#
# REGENERATED 2026-08-24, deliberately, at 476 entries from 354, after the
# socket, readiness, signal, entropy, pre-fork and checked-arithmetic work
# added nine `.ax` files to `tests/` and pushed the unpinned count past the
# ceiling of 60. Nothing about the formatter moved: the preservation and
# rebuild halves of check-fmt-selfhost.sh do not read this file and were
# green across the whole regeneration, which is what makes a re-bless here
# a record of new files rather than a formatter being made its own
# REGENERATED 2026-08-25, deliberately, after `AX3042` made an undeclared
# `IO` effect an error: 192 declarations across the compiler, the corpus and
# the standard library gained a `;@axiom:effect(io)` line, which retires a
# source hash for every file touched. Two formatter fixes land with it - an
# AXTAG inside an `(impl ...)` refused the whole file, and an ordinary
# comment inside one was re-emitted after the block it was written in.
#
# REGENERATED 2026-08-29, at 534 entries from 507. 471 of the 507 still
# matched a file, comfortably above the floor; what moved was the unpinned
# count, which the nine files the restriction work added
# (tests/diagnostics/371-378 and mods/RestrictLeaf.ax) pushed to 63 against
# the ceiling of 60 - the ceiling doing exactly what it was added for on
# 2026-08-22. Regenerated with the compiler built from this tree, per the
# recipe above.
#
#
# REGENERATED 2026-08-30, at 562 entries from 451, and the trigger was the
# margin rather than a rewrite: a clean checkout of trunk stood at 59 unpinned
# files against a ceiling of 60, so the next commit to touch six source files
# was going to cross it whatever it was. It was the AX3053 slice, which
# touched eleven. The 111 new entries are mostly the compiler's own growth -
# `self_host/` went from 64,490 lines on 2026-08-25 to 81,504 - and the count
# rises rather than churns because every previously pinned file that was not
# edited keeps its hash and its mapping.
#
# The formatter this was taken from is the one the same run proved:
# `check-fmt.sh` had just formatted all 568 `.ax` files in the tree and
# re-run every suite against the formatted copy, and this gate's own zoo and
# parity halves - which do not read this file - were green on the same binary.
# That is the evidence a re-bless needs and the reason the header above asks
# for it.
#
# REGENERATED 2026-09-02, at 585 entries from 697 - the first regeneration
# that SHRINKS the table, and the shrink is what it is for. Three things came
# off at once:
#
#   183 of the 697 keys were retired by the `(Vec a)` migration, which re-typed
#   every module in the tree and so re-hashed every source it touched. That
#   pushed the unpinned count to 71 against the ceiling of 60 - the ceiling
#   doing exactly what it was added for on 2026-08-22.
#
#   70 paths carried MORE THAN ONE key, one per edit since the last full
#   regeneration. A full regeneration keys one entry per file, so those
#   collapse: 607 distinct paths become 585.
#
#   23 paths had no file under the sweep at all. 17 are the trait fixtures
#   `efc0699` deleted; the other 6 - under `examples/` and `rust/` - are
#   outside `find stdlib self_host tests`, which is what this gate sweeps and
#   what the recipe above enumerates, so they could never be joined and only
#   inflated the entry count.
#
# THE CEILING OF 60 DOES NOT MOVE WITH THIS, and it was checked rather than
# assumed. It counts how much of the TREE is unpinned, which a full
# regeneration resets to zero by construction - 0 of 585 after this. Raising
# it to cover a decayed table would retire the one number that reported the
# decay.
#
# Verified before blessing, the check the 2026-08-22 note established: of the
# 514 source hashes present in BOTH tables, ZERO map to a different formatted
# hash. So this is a re-keying of the files the migration edited, not a
# re-blessing of a formatter that moved.
#
# `self_host/format.ax` IS edited in the commit that regenerates this, where
# the 2026-08-22 note was able to say it was not: the migration re-typed it
# like everything else - signatures gained `(Vec ...)`, and the casts moved to
# returns. No printing logic changed, and the 514-of-514 agreement above is
# the measurement of that rather than the assertion of it. The gate's other
# halves agree on the same binary and none of them reads this file: the zoo
# golden and its fixed point, all 48 parity cases, preservation over 609
# pairs (45,000 comments, 9,562 strings), and the rebuild of the compiler from
# the formatted tree reproducing the zoo golden.
#
# REGENERATED 2026-09-03, deliberately, at 602 entries from 585, because the
# UNPINNED count reached 64 against its ceiling of 60 and the gate went red
# saying so. That is the ceiling working: `26df546` (ERR-ADOPT-1), the `for`,
# `region`, `parallel`, SIMD and TCO tracks each added `.ax` files and re-typed
# others, and every edit retires an entry by construction.
#
# The ceiling caught this on the FIRST run that reached it. Run 33755288570
# died at gate 20 of 70 on a different fault, so gates 21-70 - this one among
# them - did not execute on `26df546` at all. The table had already decayed
# past the ceiling at that commit; nothing observed it until the gate ahead of
# it was fixed.
#
# Verified before blessing, the check the 2026-08-22 note established: of the
# 537 source hashes present in BOTH tables, ZERO map to a different formatted
# hash. So this is a re-keying of the files those tracks edited, not a
# re-blessing of a formatter that moved.
#
# `self_host/format.ax` is UNCHANGED in the commit that regenerates this, and
# the 537-of-537 agreement above is the measurement rather than the assertion
# of that. The gate's other halves read none of this file and agree on the same
# binary: the zoo golden and its fixed point, all 54 parity cases, preservation
# over 630 pairs (47,017 comments, 10,239 strings, 133 float magnitudes), and
# the rebuild of the compiler from the formatted tree reproducing the zoo
# golden.
#
# The 602nd entry is `tests/stdlib/472-lambda-param-class.ax`, added in the
# same commit series: the regression fixture for the lifted-lambda parameter
# misclassification. It is pinned here from birth rather than left unpinned,
# because a fixture whose whole subject is what codegen emits is exactly the
# kind of file this table exists to notice moving.
#
# THE CEILING OF 60 DOES NOT MOVE, for the reason the 2026-09-01 note gives:
# a full regeneration resets the unpinned count to zero by construction (0 of
# 602 after this), so raising the ceiling would retire the one number that
# reported the decay.
# REGENERATED 2026-09-04, deliberately, at 627 entries from 601, after ten
# concurrent streams merged onto trunk. The tree gained sixty-one `.ax` files
# that had no entry at all - new fixtures under tests/mir/, tests/axir/ and
# tests/tailpos/, `stdlib/Par.ax` replacing `stdlib/Job.ax`, and the LSP and
# examples work - which is a hole in COVERAGE rather than a decayed table: an
# unpinned file is one this gate says nothing about. The surviving entries were
# not re-blessed to make anything pass; `check-fmt-selfhost` was green on the
# 589 it still covered, and the ceiling on unpinned files (60) is what
# reported the sixty-one.
#
# 0 of 627 files are REFUSED by the formatter.
#
# REGENERATED 2026-09-04, at 627 entries from 627, and this is the FIRST
# regeneration since 1041f11 in which the FORMATTER moved rather than the
# tree: three layout defects were fixed in `self_host/format.ax` the same
# day (a broken application prints one argument per line instead of its
# indent as a run of spaces between them; a comment written first inside a
# `{ }` block stays inside it; an application headed by a qualified name lays
# out like any other). Measured before blessing, against the table as
# committed: of the 621 source hashes present in BOTH tables, 168 map to a
# different formatted hash and 453 to the same one - so 168 is the number of
# pinned files whose normal form the fix changes, and every one of them
# formats to a fixed point under the new printer (the sweep of all 634
# tracked `.ax` files refused none and changed none on a second pass). The
# other 6 keys are re-keyings: the five compiler sources edited that day
# (`format.ax`, `typecheck.ax`, `render.ax`, and `build.ax` and `lsp.ax`,
# edited at HEAD since the last regeneration) and the zoo golden itself.
#
# What holds a re-bless taken from a printer that has just moved: the zoo
# golden (`tests/fmt/syntax-zoo.expected.ax`) and the parity bank moved in
# the same commit and their diffs were READ - 9 lines of the zoo, exactly
# the three shapes above; three new parity cases, 220-222, and no older
# case's bytes - and the preservation, re-read and rebuild halves of
# `check-fmt-selfhost.sh`, which do not read this file, are green on the
# same binary.
#
# REGENERATED 2026-09-13, deliberately, at 648 entries from 627, because the
# UNPINNED count reached 64 against its ceiling of 60. That is the ceiling
# working: the nested-repeat slice (397), the arm/ctor-splice slice (398),
# the test-runner work (xfail + float-near fixtures) and the macro/expander
# edits (self_host/expand.ax, parser.ax) each retired source hashes by
# construction.
#
# Verified before blessing, the check the 2026-08-22 note established: of the
# 584 source hashes present in BOTH tables, ZERO map to a different formatted
# hash. So this is a re-keying of the files those slices edited, not a
# re-blessing of a formatter that moved.
#
# `self_host/format.ax` is UNCHANGED in the commit that regenerates this, and
# the 584-of-584 agreement above is the measurement rather than the assertion
# of that. 0 of 649 files are REFUSED by the formatter. One source hash is
# shared by two byte-identical files (tests/ddc/050-rec-sum.ax and
# tests/selfhost/050-rec.ax), so 649 files key 648 distinct entries; the
# table carries one row per distinct source hash, the path column being
# diagnostic only.
#
# REGENERATED deliberately, at 655 entries from 656 files, for the normal-form change:
# declaration heads stand alone (`fn` bodies never cuddle), `handle`
# operands go one per line, every block closer stacks onto the last
# content line, imports group without blank lines, `::` sticks to its
# `fn`, and nullary calls keep their parens. The formatter MOVED here
# by design, so the overlapping-hashes agreement above does not apply;
# what makes this re-bless safe is what does not read this file: the
# zoo and parity diffs were read line by line, preservation holds over
# every pair, idempotence holds, `check-fmt.sh` re-ran every suite
# against the formatted tree, and the rebuild reproduces the zoo.
#
# REGENERATED again the same day, keyed from the reformatted tree:
# `self_host` and `stdlib` were formatted into the new form in this
# same change, so 67 entries map a source to itself and the rest map
# an unformatted test fixture to its formatted bytes.
#
# One source hash is shared by two byte-identical files (tests/ddc/050-rec-sum.ax and
# tests/selfhost/050-rec.ax), so 656 files key 655 distinct entries; the table
# carries one row per distinct source hash, the path column being diagnostic only.
#
# REGENERATED deliberately, at 655 entries from 656 files, after formatting
# the test corpus into the stacked-closer normal form: every `.ax` file
# under `tests/` that the formatter accepts is now a fixed point of it.
# 593 of 595 test files were reformatted in place; the two that were not
# are the two CONTRIBUTING.md names as deliberately unformatted -
# `tests/fmt/syntax-zoo.ax`, the formatter's input fixture, and
# `tests/diagnostics/940-long-line.ax`, which pins a diagnostic at column
# 217 of a very long line. 653 of the 655 entries map a source to itself;
# the 2 that do not are those two files.
#
# Verified before blessing, the check the 2026-08-22 note established: of
# the 69 source hashes present in BOTH tables, ZERO map to a different
# formatted hash. So this is a re-keying of the files the reformat
# touched, not a re-blessing of a formatter that moved.
#
# `self_host/format.ax` is UNCHANGED in the commit that regenerates this,
# and the 69-of-69 agreement above is the measurement rather than the
# assertion of that. 0 of 656 files are REFUSED by the formatter. One
# source hash is shared by two byte-identical files
# (tests/ddc/050-rec-sum.ax and tests/selfhost/050-rec.ax), so 656 files
# key 655 distinct entries; the table carries one row per distinct source
# hash, the path column being diagnostic only. The gate's other halves
# read none of this file and agree on the same binary: the zoo golden
# and its fixed point, all 57 parity cases, preservation over 688 pairs,
# and the rebuild of the compiler from the formatted tree reproducing
# the zoo golden.
#
# RE-KEYED the same day for a comment-only edit to
# `tests/selfhost/465-restrict-no-wrap-runs.ax`, whose header describes
# the sweep's tagging rule and had to move with it: the entry maps the
# new source to itself like the 652 beside it, and the count above is
# unchanged.
#
# REGENERATED deliberately, at 679 entries from 680 files, for the
# `cond` removal and the variadic `if`: the compiler sources that lost
# their `cond` arms, the prelude that lost `cond2`/`cond3`, the migrated
# tests (260 and 710 under new names, the region-phi triptych, 370),
# the renamed parity case's absence from this table (`.axp` files are
# not swept), and the four new files (the 1000-case pair, `DefScopeWalk`,
# and the two `cond`-refusal diagnostics, which the formatter REFUSES -
# the first REFUSED rows this table has ever carried). One source hash
# is still shared by two byte-identical files, so 680 files key
# 679 entries.
#
# Verified before blessing, the check the 2026-08-22 note established:
# of the 633 source hashes present in BOTH tables, ZERO map to a
# different formatted hash. So this is a re-keying of the files the
# removal touched, not a re-blessing of a formatter that moved.
# `self_host/format.ax`'s only behavior change is the new `fpIf` arm
# for five or more operands (three still print exactly as before -
# the zoo golden, byte-identical outside its one rewritten section,
# is the measurement of that) and the `cond` refusal.
#
# REGENERATED 2026-09-21, deliberately, at 683 entries from 679, after
# `Unsafe` inference joined the effect rows: the checker sources, the
# `effect(unsafe)` tags across the tests, the `restrict(no-unsafe)`
# help text, and the `pure` tag the syntax zoo's `counted` could no
# longer carry retired 61 source hashes and pushed the unpinned count
# past the ceiling of 60.
#
# Verified before blessing, the check the 2026-08-22 note established:
# of the 622 source hashes present in BOTH tables, ZERO map to a
# different formatted hash (the one apparent move is a path alias over
# byte-identical files). So this is a re-keying of the files the
# inference touched, not a re-blessing of a formatter that moved.
# `self_host/format.ax` is unchanged.
#
